---
// src/pages/legal/disclaimer.astro
import LegalLayout from '../../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../../data/site';
---
<LegalLayout
  title="Disclaimer"
  description="Important clarifications about the forward-looking nature of this site, the treatment of gifts, the limits of what is offered here, and where to find help in a crisis."
  updated="30 July 2026"
  intro="We would rather say less and mean it than say more and overstate. This page sets out what this site is — and what it is not."
>
  <h2>A ministry in formation</h2>
  <p>
    Ember Ridge is a vision under active discernment and development. The property
    described on this site has not been acquired, and the buildings described — including
    the worship pavilion, prayer garden, and leadership residence — have not been designed,
    permitted, or built. References to acquisition, renovation, or construction describe
    intentions, not completed facts.
  </p>

  <h2>Concept images</h2>
  <p>
    Images on this site identified as concepts are design references. They do not depict
    the property in its current condition, they are not architectural drawings, and they
    are not representations of what will be built. Dimensions shown in concept material
    are preliminary and subject to survey, engineering, zoning, and final design.
  </p>

  <h2>Forward-looking statements</h2>
  <p>
    Statements about future plans, timelines, capacity, programs, staffing, or budgets are
    based on present information and prayerful judgment. They may change materially as
    appraisal, inspection, survey, engineering, zoning, contractor pricing, board approval,
    funding, and circumstances direct. Nothing here should be relied upon as a promise of
    a future outcome.
  </p>

  <h2>Financial figures</h2>
  <p>
    Capital figures published on this site are preliminary planning ranges. They are not
    appraisals or guaranteed project costs, and they will be revised as real information is
    received. No representation is made that any project will be completed at a stated
    cost, on a stated schedule, or at all.
  </p>
  <p>
    Nothing on this site is an offer to sell or a solicitation of an offer to buy any
    security, partnership interest, or interest in real property.
  </p>

  <h2>Gifts and tax treatment</h2>
  <p>
    Firebrand Revivalists is a church within the meaning of section 508(c)(1)(A) of the
    Internal Revenue Code. Gifts are tax-deductible to the extent permitted by law, and
    giving receipts are provided.
  </p>
  <p>
    Under IRS Publication 1771, a donor must obtain a contemporaneous written
    acknowledgment from the recipient organization to claim a deduction for any single
    contribution of $250 or more, and organizations must provide a written disclosure when
    a donor makes a quid pro quo contribution over $75 — that is, a payment made partly as
    a gift and partly in exchange for goods or services.
  </p>
  <p>
    Gifts are voluntary, irrevocable, and non-refundable once received. Gifts designated
    for Ember Ridge are tracked to that purpose, subject to the governing body’s ultimate
    authority over the use of contributed funds as described in our
    <a href="/legal/terms-of-use">Terms of Use</a>.
  </p>
  <p>
    We do not provide tax advice. Deductibility depends on your individual circumstances.
    Please consult your own tax professional.
  </p>

  <h2>No professional advice</h2>
  <p>
    Content on this site — including teaching, testimony, and written material — is offered
    for information and spiritual encouragement. It is not legal, financial, tax,
    accounting, medical, psychiatric, psychological, or counseling advice. Reading this
    site or contacting us does not create an attorney-client, therapist-client, pastoral
    counseling, or other professional relationship.
  </p>
  <p>
    Members of the leadership team hold professional credentials. Any professional services
    they may provide in another capacity are separate from this ministry, are governed by
    their own engagement agreements, and are not offered through this website. Descriptions
    of professional background are biographical and are not an offer of services.
  </p>

  <h2>Ministry, healing, and medical care</h2>
  <p>
    We believe God heals and restores. We also believe He works through physicians,
    counselors, and other qualified professionals. Nothing on this site should be
    understood as encouragement to discontinue medical or mental health treatment, to
    delay professional care, or to substitute prayer for necessary medical attention.
  </p>
  <p>
    Prayer offered by this ministry is not a diagnosis, treatment, or guarantee of any
    particular outcome. Testimonies describe individual experiences and are not
    representations of what anyone else should expect.
  </p>

  <h2>Crisis and emergencies</h2>
  <p>
    This website and its contact form are not monitored continuously and are not an
    emergency service. If you are in immediate danger, contact local emergency services. In
    the United States, the 988 Suicide &amp; Crisis Lifeline can be reached by calling or
    texting <strong>988</strong>.
  </p>

  <h2>Historical and prophetic references</h2>
  <p>
    This site references historical accounts — including the Moravian prayer watch at
    Herrnhut, testimonies associated with Prayer Mountain and Moravian Falls, the Golden
    Candlestick fellowship, and a 1997 prophetic word concerning the area — as part of the
    spiritual testimony of the region. We receive such accounts with gratitude while
    keeping Scripture, humility, and wise discernment at the center. We do not present them
    as verified claims about present or future events, and we make no claim that any
    location produces spiritual results.
  </p>

  <h2>Third-party content</h2>
  <p>
    Links to other organizations and services are provided for convenience. We do not
    control them and are not responsible for their content, practices, or availability. A
    link is not an endorsement.
  </p>

  <h2>Accuracy</h2>
  <p>
    We work to keep this site accurate and current, but we do not warrant that it is free
    of errors or omissions, and we may correct or update content at any time without
    notice.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Ember Ridge, a ministry of Firebrand Revivalists<br />
    Moravian Falls, North Carolina<br />
    <a href={`mailto:${site.contact.email}`}>{site.contact.email}</a>
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
